                <pb facs="0604" n="522" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg522"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2506.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Nuevo
                            Laredo to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nuevo Laredo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-11-18"><hi rendition="#italic">November 18,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Gen. Bernardo Reyes and other revolutionists and the sheriff of Webb County,
                    Tex., were arrested to-day for violation of the neutrality laws. Every vestige
                    of the revolution will be swept away in 10 days if this method is followed and
                    if revolutionary property is confiscated.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
